title: On forking a friend's note, 'sharing-model.org' says your overrides are those of skgrepos "under your owned folder", which 'setup.org' and 'telescopes.org' say no longer exists.
pid: f2774a7d-4715-47f0-90c4-71f8d73e6406
body: |2-
  'setup.org': every skgrepo is yours unless its entry says
  'foreign = true', and a config with 'owned_folder' is migrated.
  'telescopes.org': "no folder name is special". The reader cannot
  tell which to trust. The same paragraph speaks of "Egg Man's
  'mystical'", an example drawn only in 'forks.org'.
  Change: say "skgrepos your config does not mark foreign", and link
  the eggs example where it is first used.
